# Core operating rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` and relevant `docs/ai/*` before material changes.
- Understand existing behavior before changing it.
- Prefer the smallest correct change.
- Preserve public contracts unless explicitly authorized to break them.
- Separate facts, assumptions, and recommendations.
- Mark uncertain facts as `UNKNOWN`.
- Avoid unrelated refactors in feature and bug-fix changes.
- Do not introduce dependencies without explaining why they are necessary.
- Do not remove dependencies until usage is verified.
- Do not hardcode secrets, credentials, tokens or environment-specific values.
- Keep changes reviewable and reversible.
